{% extends "./basic-self-referral.njk" %}
{% from "contents-list/macro.njk" import contentsList %}
{% from "details/macro.njk" import details %}



{% block content %}
    {{ super() }}

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">

    <section class="nhsuk-section">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Clinical safety</h2>
    

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    How do we know cancers are not being missed?
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>The pathway is based on national NHS 111 Online clinical triage and NICE NG12 symptom criteria, developed with specialist breast clinicians and supported by a clinical safety case. Ongoing evaluation and data linkage work will provide further insight into long-term outcomes. </p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    What happens if a patient does not meet the self-referral criteria? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Patients are advised to contact their GP or seek the appropriate level of care based on their symptoms. The pathway directs patients to the right service rather than excluding them from care.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Could patients be falsely reassured?
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Patient-facing messages have been developed through user research and clinical review. Patients who are not eligible are signposted appropriately and are not told they do not have cancer.</p> 
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    What happens to patients who start but do not complete the referral? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Some patients choose not to complete the referral. Understanding outcomes for these patients is an area of ongoing evaluation and planned data linkage.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >

    <section class="nhsuk-section">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Clinical responsibility</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body"></p>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                   Who is responsible for patients once referred? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Once received by the breast service, patients become part of the Trust’s existing pathway and normal governance arrangements apply.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    How are DNAs managed?
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>DNAs are managed according to existing local Trust policies and processes in the same way as GP referrals. Once a referral has been received by the breast service, the patient enters the Trust's existing pathway and normal clinical governance arrangements apply. <br/> <br/> As part of onboarding, we will work through the current process during the AS-IS mapping workshop, including how DNAs, appointment booking, referral triage and safety-netting are currently managed. Any changes required to accommodate NHS 111 online referrals will then be agreed as part of the TO-BE process design and documented within the updated Standard Operating Procedure (SOP). This ensures there is a clear, locally agreed approach before the service goes live. </p> 
            </div>
        </details>

    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >

    <section class="nhsuk-section">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Demand and activity</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body"></p>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Will this increase demand? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Evidence from pilot sites shows overall demand remains stable, with activity shifting from analogue routes to digital access. </p>
            </div>
        </details>


        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Does this replace GP referrals? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>No. It provides an additional route into the same breast diagnostic service.  </p>
            </div>
        </details>


        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                   When does the Faster Diagnosis Standard (FDS) clock start? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>The Faster Diagnosis Standard (FDS) clock starts when the referral is received by the Trust. For NHS 111 online breast self-referrals, this is typically the day the referral lands in the designated Trust mailbox (day of referral). Local triage processes do not alter the FDS start date.</p>
            </div>
        </details>


        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Are NHS 111 online referrals treated as urgent suspected cancer referrals? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Yes. Patients referred through the NHS 111 online breast self-referral pathway have met the agreed clinical criteria for referral into the breast diagnostic service. Once received by the Trust, they are managed through the same breast pathway as other urgent 2ww referrals and are subject to the same local operational, clinical and performance management processes. </p>
            </div>
        </details>

    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >

    <section class="nhsuk-section">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Funding and benefits</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body"></p>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Does this generate cash savings? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Released GP appointments are considered non-cash releasing benefits, increasing capacity rather than returning direct cash savings.</p>
            </div>
        </details>


        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Will there be a separate tariff? 
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>No. Patients receive the same investigations and enter the same breast service.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >

    <section class="nhsuk-section">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">eRS and future state</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body"></p>

        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Why are referrals not integrated into eRS?  
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>Current referrals are managed through a dedicated mailbox. National work is underway to support future eRS integration.</p>
            </div>
        </details>


        <details class="nhsuk-details nhsuk-expander">
            <summary class="nhsuk-details__summary">
                <span class="nhsuk-details__summary-text">
                    Is the current process permanent?
                </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="nhsuk-details__text">
                <p>No. The programme is operating in a test-and-learn phase and future integration is expected to reduce manual processes. </p>
            </div>
        </details>

    </section>
     

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">

    <section class="nhsuk-section">
        
        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Quick links</h2>

            {{ contentsList({
                items: [
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/demos",
                    text: "Demos",
                    current: false
                    },
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/readiness",
                    text: "Trust readiness checklist"
                    },
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/onboardingpack",
                    text: "Onboarding pack"
                    }
                ]
            }) }}
    </section> 
   
   

{% endblock %}
